{title: Jingle Bells}
{artist: James Lord Pierpont}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 120}
{meta: public_domain Words and music by James Lord Pierpont, published 1857 as "One Horse Open Sleigh" and reissued 1859 as "Jingle Bells".}
{meta: source Sheet music, Oliver Ditson & Co., Boston, 1857 and 1859.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Dashing through the snow
In a [C]one-horse open [G]sleigh,
O'er the [G]fields we go,
[D]Laughing all the [G]way;
Bells on [G]bob-tail ring,
Making [C]spirits [G]bright,
What [C]fun it is to [G]ride and sing
A [D]sleighing song to[D7]night!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Jingle bells, [G]jingle bells,
[G]Jingle all the [G]way,
[C]Oh what fun it [G]is to ride
In a [A7]one-horse open [D7]sleigh!
[G]Jingle bells, [G]jingle bells,
[G]Jingle all the [G]way,
[C]Oh what fun it [G]is to ride
In a [D7]one-horse open [G]sleigh!
{end_of_chorus}
